  "hard_limits": [
    "Actual unmodified 2.5 effect resources and dependency graphs have not been supplied to this subtask. Third-party modified assets are not vanilla evidence.",
    "A ColorGrade track may contain contrast/saturation/brightness alongside a LUT; deleting the entire track can remove more than the blue filter.",
    "ColorGradeV2 does not expose the same LUT fields as ColorGrade; identifying the blue contribution requires actual resource data.",
    "ArchiveXL copy reads whichever source resource wins the depot; installed third-party overrides must be excluded before calling it a vanilla copy.",
    "Preserving native enter/loop/exit timing requires routing original event requests/transitions, not a polling-driven substitute playback.",
    "No game 2.5 compile, resource instance identity, native lookup or GPU render tests were run."
  ],
  "recommendation": "Do not modify shared depot resource. Investigate a private resource.copy from verified vanilla paths, inspect those complete resources, neutralize only a positively identified blue LUT contribution, and route original CHRONOS native event lifecycle to private counterparts. Until the actual graph and routing are known, do not publish a FULL ZIP claiming exact vanilla parity.",
  "runtime_validation_required": [
    "Verify private copy token path/resource identity and all mutable graph nodes are isolated from original before editing.",
    "Inspect exact user-2.5 vanilla ColorGrade/material inputs; preserve contrast/saturation/brightness and other non-blue parameters.",
    "Do not infer independence just from a changed resource.path field or Clone returning a different top-level handle.",
    "Ensure native enter/persistent/exit event routing and blackboard/lifecycle context are preserved; do not Stop/replace with polling playback.",
